//Haley Storme & Tailgating Terror
//First Place Forecasts
RadioStation.Weather : nonoverlap_pool
{
	//"\1\b[20]wow the weather sure is hot!"
	
	//Weather
	_sunnyskies = ("sunny skies","cloudy skies","showers","the worms","sniffles and sneezes","electric zaps","psionic bolts")[Weather.Today]
	"\1\b[22]The latest weather data is in: %(_sunnyskies) are here to stay throughout the afternoon! Stay tuned for the details on how we expect this to affect the air quality, your commute, and SO much more, here on \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default]!"
	"\1\b[22]If you look outside your window, you can expect to see %(_sunnyskies) today! That's mother nature's way of reminding us that SHE is in charge! Isn't that awesome!?\n\n If you're enthusiastic about weather, stay tuned, because we'll have lots more detail for you right after this word from our sponsors!"
	"\1\b[22]We've got a LOT of weather to talk about today, this show is going to be EXCITING for the next hour!\n\n This is Haley Storme, reporting for%(br)\f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default], and if you're not excited about seeing %(_sunnyskies) today then YOU SHOULD BE, and we're gonna talk about why!"
	
	_sunsunsun = ("sun, sun, sun","thickly clouded skies","heavy rainstorms","just the right conditions for the worm migration","extra breezy, picking up allergens such as pollen and dust and carrying them everywhere","electrifying, with jolts of raw electric power crackling in the air","full of intense bolts of energy as slugs everywhere exercise their psionic powers")[Weather.Today]
	"\1\b[22]The weather today is going to be %(_sunsunsun) all through the afternoon and going into the evening, and if THAT doesn't excite you I don't know what will!"
	
	{
		"\1\b[22]And NOW it's time for this hour's FIRSTHAND weather report, courtesy of me, your host Haley Storme!\n\n That's right, at \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] we don't JUST read out the data to you from our weather stations placed strategically across the whole continent, we put our money where our mouth is! And THAT means going outside to get a feel for the weather ourselves!\n\n "
		--
		switch Weather.Today
		{
			"The sun sure was hot as I stepped out the studio doors and into its powerful rays, and let me tell you, it was an INTENSE experience! There's NOTHING more powerful than the sun, isn't that so awesome!? That's the kind of power we should all be reverent of!\n\n And with that in mind, I was dragged back into the studio and made to apply vigorous amounts of sunscreen. Don't forget your sunscreen today, people; the sun will burn you to a crisp if you underestimate it!"
			"We've got a great view of the skies from the front door of our studio, and let me tell you, they sure are CLOUDY today! With my own eyes I saw a thick blanket across the sky, with all those lovely fluffy cloud textures that make it look so cozy.\n\n And the colors! Don't forget about the colors. The cloud cover ranged from a light blueish white to a dark purple-y gray, and I'm sure there will be many more vibrant colors later this evening as the sun sets! The clouds really know how to put on a good light show! So get out there and see the skies TODAY!"
			"The rain was pouring down as I stepped out of the studio, and a stiff breeze brought the rain right to me even though I was under the awning. I couldn't resist after that, I ran out headlong into the torrent and held my hands up to the sky, letting it soak me right through!\n\n Lightning flashed, thunder rumbled, and the winds blew harder and harder. What a rush! Nature is really awe-inspiring, isn't it!?\n\n I almost didn't come back inside to deliver this report, except that the studio manager came running out with an umbrella and brought me back in. I'm telling you here and now, go out and experience that storm before it's GONE!"
			"I didn't get two steps outside the studio before seeing worms EVERYWHERE, worming their way along to their new homes! Isn't that amazing? When the humidity is perfect and the temperature is about right, out they come in droves!\n\n I tried to pick my way across the walkway to see around the side of the building, but it was so crowded I couldn't make it without risking stepping on the worms! So I came back inside and decided to look from our 2nd floor observatory.\n\n If you've not gone out to see them yet, make sure you do, but plan your route carefully!"
			"Let me tell you what I saw the moment I stepped out the door. Ripples of wind tearing through the grass, flowers bobbing to and fro scattering their pollen, dandelion puffs soaring through the air%(emdash) it was amazing! Bees and butterflies were out in droves, making sure to spread that pollen around. What hard workers they are!\n\n Many of our dear helper snails around the studio were snuffling and sneezing,%(br)but like the true champions they are, they've committed to bringing you the weather NO MATTER WHAT!\n\n The weather sure is amazing, and so are the snails that help us bring it to you!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[color,disable]\f[italic,1]K-chuu!\f[italic,default]\f[color,default]" //TODO do we want to use the snail graphics here or save that for bill and blanca/pirate radio lol
			"Today I stepped outside with a handful of dead batteries. You know the kind! Not enough power for even a remote control!\n\n The first thing I noticed was my hair starting to stand on end, and then I heard a crackle nearby that made me jump! Ooh, the tingling feelings were INTENSE!\n\n After a few minutes of this, I pulled out my battery tester and got to checking those batteries, and wouldn't you know it%(emdash) they were perfectly charged! Completely full, ready for a new life! Thanks, mother nature!"
			"I always take precautions on a day like today, and so I had my trusty tinfoil hat on as I stepped outside the studio door. I'm glad I did, because as soon as I was outside, I could feel some kind of presence all around me!\n\n It was like there were a thousand eyes on me, and I got really intense goosebumps! I wonder if there was a slug nearby!? But thanks to the power of my hat, I felt no pressure on my brain at all. My thoughts were safe!\n\n The snail crew that works in the studio didn't have protection, so they shied away from the door, understandably. But if you have the proper equipment to experience a psionic storm safely, it's a feeling like no other! Shifts of energy; walking through focal points and feeling vast amounts of attention on you; the undeniable sensation that you're being followed wherever you go! No weather enthusiast's experience is complete until they've tried it."
		}
	}
	
	//Weather, but fully different
	if Weather.Today == 0 //Sunny
	{
		"\1\b[22]The sun's rays are HOT today. If you're going out, be sure to bring sunscreen for you, and a misting bottle for your snail! At these temperatures, snails might be inclined to go into estivation, so it's important to keep them cool and moist while you're outdoors!"
		"\1\b[22]If you like sunglasses, today is your day to SHINE! Rock those shades everywhere you go today, because that sun is BRIGHT.\n\n If you haven't got your snail a pair, make sure to do that as well! Snails eyes deserve to be shaded too, and they'll love feeling cool alongside you!"
		"\1\b[22]If you head outside right about now, you will be absolutely BOMBARDED with ultraviolet rays. That's the sun at work, showing off its incredible power! NO other weather event on Earth beats it, not even close!"
		"\1\b[22]If you're heading out today, bring your sun gear! Sunscreen, umbrellas, mist bottles, squirt guns, plenty of drinking water, all of it!\n\n Experiencing the sun is GREAT, but you probably don't want to experience heat stroke too!" //"probably"
		"\1\b[22]If you're planning to spend the day tanning, remember to leave your snails at home! Or if they must come along, provide them with PLENTY of shade and cool water.\n\n Snails don't tan, and they don't take well to the heat, so you're better off not making them try!"
		
		"\1\b[22]If you're running errands with your snail today, make sure you don't leave it in your car, or you might return to find escargot! Cars in the sun are practically OVENS, so be careful with your snails today, or find a different mode of transport!"
		"\1\b[22]All this sun is GREAT for the lettuce crops that are still growing! The sun may be powerful, but plants EAT that power up for themselves, turning it into something we can use! So cool, right!?"
		"\1\b[22]It's a tanktop and sunglasses kind of day, no need for a jacket of ANY kind! Unless you consider sunscreen to be a jacket, but why would you!?\n\n Get out there and enjoy the warm weather while it's here! Unless you don't like warm weather, in which case, stay inside and crank that A/C up!"
		"\1\b[22]Today would be a GREAT day to invest in a personal fan! Whether it's a floor unit for your home, or a hand unit to hold, fans are a great way to beat the heat without breaking the bank!\n\n And as a sweet bonus, a fan can double as a training exercise for your snails! Point the fan at them to simulate INTENSE wind conditions, and help them build up their resilience!"
		"\1\b[22]Need some ideas to beat the heat? You might consider for a walk where there are lots of trees to provide shade, or visit a nearby waterpark! You can ALSO try your community's swimming pool, or there are jumbo spray bottles for sale if you want to match with your snail and use a few quick spritzes to cool down!"
	}
	elseif Weather.Today == 1 //Cloudy
	{
		"\1\b[22]If you like shade and milder temperatures, today's the day to be outside, because the cloud cover is THICK! No storms yet though; these clouds are storm-free and are just here to say hello!"
		"\1\b[22]Whenever I see cloudy skies like this, I always think to myself that it's like the Earth is wrapped in a cozy blanket.%(br)Isn't that so cool?\n\n I want a blanket made of clouds, too! Someone should invent that. If there's an inventor out there listening, it could be YOU that makes the dreams of so many weather enthusiasts come true!"
		"\1\b[22]Today is a great day to get outdoors and go play at the park with your snails. Play some catch, have a casual race, maybe bring some lettuce and have a picnic!\n\n Whatever you end up doing, you won't need any special gear to get the most out of today!"
		"\1\b[22]I spent my lunch break today cloudwatching, and you'll NEVER believe what I saw. A cloud shaped just like %(acloudsnail)! Isn't that amazing!? It was so detailed!\n\n If you go out cloudwatching today, make sure you share what you saw on our website! We'd love to get a clearer picture on what people are seeing in the clouds!"
		"\1\b[22]Have you ever wished you could touch a cloud!? I have! Unfortunately, I haven't had the opportunity to actually do it yet, but you CAN buy cloud flavored cotton candy, and that's almost as good!\n\n I'm told one of the ingredients is really harvested from clouds, too, so this stuff is the real deal! If you're a cloud enthusiast, you owe it to yourself to try it!" //This kinda feels like it should be one of the sponsored segments, but it's kind of specific to this weather...??? hmm
		
		"\1\b[22]Along with the clouds today, there is a lovely breeze out to chase away the heat! You might consider bringing a light jacket or sweater when you head out, if you're particularly sensitive to cooler temperatures.\n\n Your snails will LOVE this kind of weather, so this is a great time to get them outside for some fun and exercise!"
		"\1\b[22]I wish I could be a cloud... \w8\w8\n\n ... Huh? We're LIVE!?\n\n U-uh, have you seen the clouds outside today!? There's a lot of them! All kinds of shapes, and a variety of grays, with a lot of blue-grays! Isn't that neat!?"
		"\1\b[22]Cloudy days like this get one of my favorite weather phenomena: sunbeams! If you look in just the right place at just the right time, you'll see beautiful beams of light stretching down from the sky, lighting up a whole township!"
		"\1\b[22]The nice cool temperatures we're getting today are brought to you by clouds! Puffy, white or gray, AND available in a variety of shapes and sizes, clouds are wonderful and truly a boon for those of us living on the ground!\n\n The sun is remarkably strong, constantly battering the Earth with POWERFUL rays of light, trying to turn us all into one big serving of escargot. And yet, the humble cloud is able to deflect much of its light away, letting us continue on with our lives! Truly astonishing, everyone give a hearty round of applause to our friends, clouds!"
		"\1\b[22]What's hiding above the clouds!? Some experts speculate that %(floatingcities) may be secreted away up there!\n\n What do YOU think? Vote on our website, or send in your own theories for us to investigate!"
	}
	elseif Weather.Today == 2 //Rainy
	{
		"\1\b[22]The storms are expected to ease up this next hour, and we'll be seeing a light rain for a while before the thicker clouds move in.\n\n If you're looking to get soaked without getting blown away by the wind, this will be the PERFECT chance to head out and experience the wonder of nature firsthand!"
		"\1\b[22]Ooh, there goes another bolt of lightning! Aren't thunderstorms SO much fun to watch!?\n\n We'll be uploading slow-motion shots of some of the lightning to our website later, so be sure to check it out!"
		"\1\b[22]If you're heading out today and need to stay dry, don't forget your umbrella!\n\n \w8\w8But if you've got nowhere to be, then go ahead and stand outside without for a while. It is THE prime rainstorm experience!"
		"\1\b[22]The rain is showing no signs of letting up, and in a few hours, it'll be the PERFECT conditions to stomp around in rain boots and splash in puddles. Make sure you've got your gear together to take advantage of this opportunity while it's here!"
		"\1\b[22]If you don't have time to get out and experience the rain today, then try today's \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] Weather Pro Tip%(tm)! Stick a jar or jug OUTSIDE where it will get rained on, and let it collect rainwater while you go about your day. Then when you have some spare time, you've got your own PERSONAL STASH of rain to experience!"
		
		"\1\b[22]Today is a great day to bust out all of those rainy day activities you've been saving up! Board games, cleaning, WHATEVER you've got on your list, you've got time, so get to it!\n\n Of course, if you're a rain enthusiast like myself, then this might be a busy day for you! And if that's you, then good luck and make the most of it!"
		"\1\b[22]If you're like me, the sound of that pitter-patter on the windows will have you yearning to finish up work and get OUTSIDE where the RAIN is. Being stuck inside where it's dry can be MISERABLE!\n\n But don't worry! The rain is certain to continue throughout the afternoon and evening, so you'll have PLENTY of time to get out there and soak it up!"
		"\1\b[22]Don't forget to thank the friendly clouds today that are bringing us ALL this rain!\n\n Thank you, clouds! What would we do without you!?"
		"\1\b[22]If you're heading outside in this next hour, hold onto your umbrella TIGHT if you have one! The wind speeds are picking up, and your umbrella might just get carried away if you're not careful!"
		"\1\b[22]Make sure to keep an eye on your snails today! A lot of snails love rainfall, so they might sneak outside if you're not careful.\n\n Experts say the best thing to do is plan some outside time with your snail during each storm, so it doesn't feel the need to sneak out just to experience it! It'll be safer for your snail, AND you get some extra bonding time!"
	}
	elseif Weather.Today == 3 //Wormy
	{
		"\1\b[22]The worms just KEEP on COMING today! They've carved a little worm river across our parking lot, and are wriggling their way steadily across.\n\n No matter where you are, the worm migration is ALWAYS a sight to behold!"
		"\1\b[22]If you like worms, then today is your lucky day, because if you step outside you'll see THOUSANDS of them! Rivers of worms have appeared across every community as the worms migrate to a new home.\n\n If you're lucky, their new chosen home might be right outside yours! If you're a worm fan, that would SURELY be a dream come true."
		"\1\b[22]Our dedicated Worm Team has been hard at work mapping out the paths of the worm migration, and you can see the results of their efforts up on our site! If you're into following worm paths and tracking their behaviors, it's an invaluable tool that you should make use of.\n\n And if you've found any worm paths that we've missed, let us know and we'll dispatch someone to check it out and add it to our map if it's found to be legitimate!"
		"\1\b[22]It looks like I'll be working overtime today. One of the worm paths from today's migration is going DIRECTLY over my car, Hahaha!\n\n I couldn't possibly move it without crushing SEVERAL worms and very likely breaking their path, so I guess I'll either have to camp out here tonight or find another way home!"
		"\1\b[22]Oh! It looks like a lost little worm has somehow found its way inside our studio! This isn't where you're meant to be, little guy!\n\n \w8\w8\f[color,disable]Can someone get this worm back outside with the others, please?\f[color,default]\n\n \w8\w8\w8\w8Well! That sure was a cute diversion, but we've GOT to get BACK to the forecast!"
		
		//Dr. Wormington
		"\1\b[22]The worms sure know how to seize the day when the conditions are just right! One has to wonder how they know to all get up and migrate as if on cue. And we REALLY wanted to know, so today we're asking Dr.\![] Earth Wormington, an expert on the subject, that very question! Dr.\![] Wormington, how is it that the worms manage to coordinate such an effort perfectly every time!?\n\n Well, now, that, see, that we're not really sure. Not yet. But the research so far is leading us to conclude that, well, it may be that the worms have some sort of ""hive mind"" link.\n\n You're kidding!? That would TOTALLY explain it! You could certainly NEVER get humans to coordinate on that scale, and maybe not even snails.\n\n Well, yes, that's why we're exploring that theory. But the, uh, the research, it's still in a preliminary phase. We can't say anything concretely just yet, so, please treat it as only a theory.\n\n Man, I can't WAIT to tell my bestie about THIS! She's the world's #1 worm enthusiast, she'll be ECSTATIC to hear a new worm fact!!"
		"\1\b[22]THIS JUST IN: If worms are considered a weather phenomenon, shouldn't snails be considered one too!? Dr.\![] Earth Wormington, you're an expert in worm research. What do you think about this question that's been raised as of late?\n\n Well, you see, uh, that is, the worms \f[italic,1]do\f[italic,default] have a specific weather-based component. They only come out to migrate when the weather conditions are perfect, so, it's not really like snails at all, since snails are ever-present in our environment.\n\n But Dr.\![] Wormington, couldn't one make the argument that snails DO have a weather based component, since they both hibernate and estivate?\n\n Well, that's, well... that's... It's, it's really a very different thing. Each snail does or does not do those things based on the conditions it is personally in, but the worms act as one, more like a weather phenomenon. That's, well, that's why they're classed as one.\n\n I see! So in the end, the worms might as well be weather since they act SO much like it!"
		"\1\b[22]For all your worm-related questions, we've got Dr.\![] Earth Wormington on today! Dr.\![] Wormington, one of our listeners wants to know why exactly it is that the worms migrate so much!?\n\n Well, that's, uh, it's actually a very interesting field of study all on its own. You see, we can't talk to worms, and uh, if they're kept in a lab environment they don't behave like normal worms. So we really have to study them, well, out in the field, which introduces many more variables.\n\n Got it, got it... so do you have any leading theories?\n\n Well, you see, we think that the worms, perhaps, might simply be dissatisfied with their homes. It could very well be be that they've used up certain nutrients in the soil, or the moisture isn't quite right, or maybe they just couldn't get it decorated how they wanted. And so, when the conditions are right, well, they up and move again.\n\n Wow! It sounds TOUGH to be a worm, never staying in the same place for very long! Although now that you say it, maybe I should consider moving too... I could finally leave that tacky lamp behind me! I think I suddenly understand worms on a level I never have before."
		"\1\b[22]Time for some new worm knowledge! We've got Dr.\![] Earth Wormington in the studio today, here to answer another listener question. Dr.\![] Wormington, is it true that if you cut a worm in half, each half will turn into a whole new worm!?\n\n Well, it's, it's really rather complicated of a topic. It depends a lot on which kind of worm you're talking about, and as I don't, uh, know what kind of worms your curious listener has in their possession, then I would have to encourage them to do their own research into the subject based on the type of worm they have.\n\n Ohh, that sounds like fun! I might just try doing some research myself later today when I go home, hahaha!" //don't cut worms in half lol
		"\1\b[22]It's worm time, and that means we've got Dr.\![] Earth Wormington on the show with us today to answer ALL of your worm-related questions! Dr.\![] Wormington, some of our listeners have expressed interest in keeping worms as pets. They want to know, what do you FEED a worm!?\n\n Well, that is, well. It can be done, but it's best not to keep worms indoors. Indoor worms don't behave like outdoor worms, and will miss out on important worm things such as the worm migrations. So really, I'd, I'd recommend that your listeners simply don't keep worms at all.\n\n Aw, well that's a shame. Sorry to the listeners who sent that one in! You'll have to settle for watching the worms in the wild, instead!"
	}
	elseif Weather.Today == 4 //Sneezy
	{
		"\1\b[22]I don't know about you, but I don't even have to look outside today to know how the weather is! Several of our poor helper snails in the studio today have red, itchy eyes, and have been snuffling and sneezing all day.\n\n If that description sounds like it fits YOUR snail, then your snail likely has allergies! The recommendation for today is to keep it indoors, and find some relaxing activities to do or tasty treats to eat."
		"\1\b[22]That strong breeze can only mean one thing%(emdash) POLLEN! Pollen EVERYWHERE! If you or your snails have allergies, this would be a good day to stay inside and do some indoor activities!"
		"\1\b[22]The allergens in the air today are so strong that even the TREES are sneezing! On my way in today, I saw a puff of white come out of one and rain down all over the people underneath it. The poor thing! Imagine how hard it must be to be allergic to YOUR OWN pollen!"
		"\1\b[22]If you've got allergies, this is a bad day to go out! Call out of work sick if you have to, the pollen levels are in the EXTREME!\n\n Of course, if you're a flower, then this is a great day for you, hahaha!"
		"\1\b[22]The winds really picked up this morning, and they're expected to keep going strong throughout the afternoon and evening, spreading pollen far and wide! If you or your snails have allergies, try to stay indoors if at all possible. Your errands can WAIT until it's over!"
		
		"\1\b[22]Do you hear that? That's the sound of a sneezy snail, and that's how you know it's sneezy out today!\n\n That warm breeze is carrying allergens to and fro without a care in the world, and unfortunately our dear snail friends are suffering for it. If you've got a sneezy snail today, try giving it a treat to help make up for the weather!"
		"\1\b[22]The temperature today is just right with how breezy it is today. It's a good day to take a hike, walk around the park, OR do some sort of other outdoor activity!\n\n ... That is, if you don't have allergies! If you have allergies, then today is a WRECK and you should stay indoors as much as possible!"
		
		//Dr. Hayes Fever
		"\1\b[22]With all the pollen in the air today, we've brought on a specialist, Dr.\![] Hayes Fever, to discuss how to best take care of your snails! Dr.\![] Hayes, what's your #1 snail care tip on a day like today?\n\n Certainly. The best thing you can do for your snails is to give them a thorough shell wash tomorrow.\n\n A shell wash?\n\n Yes. Pollen drifts through the air and can stick to surfaces, so your snails can continue reacting to the pollen even after the weather has calmed down! It's best to wash their shells once things are back to normal to get rid of any lingering allergens.\n\n Oh, wow! I'd NEVER have thought of that! That just goes to show you folks, experts really know what they're talking about!"
		"\1\b[22]Some of our listeners have been asking questions related to allergies, due to the high pollen counts in the air today. Dr.\![] Hayes, you're an expert in the subject, so maybe YOU have an answer for this: why is it that some snails have allergies and others don't?\n\n Genetics.\n\n ... Oh, is that all?\n\n Yep. Some snails are just born with an intolerance. But, it can be reduced over time with certain therapeutic treatments.\n\n Oh, how interesting! I had NO idea it was treatable!\n\n Yes, many people are unaware of this possibility. But it does work, and you should try it! It will greatly improve the quality of life of your snails."
		"\1\b[22]Today on the show we've got Dr.\![] Hayes Fever, a renowned allergist, here to talk about the impact of this sneezy weather on our dear snails! Dr.\![] Hayes, our listeners want to know, what's the best way they can increase the comfort of their snails at home?\n\n One of the most effective methods is to simply keep as much outdoor air outside of your home as you possibly can until the winds die down. Close all your windows, make sure your doors fit snugly and that you've sealed any drafts, and have a good filter on your HVAC system to remove pollen particles from the indoor air as it circulates around.\n\n Ohh... those are all GREAT tips!\n\n Yes, this is better done in advance, but some of it you can start implementing today. Another thing to do is to try and not go outside too much today; every time you open your door, more allergens have the chance to get inside, which you really don't want. So sit tight and wait it out, and then gather up supplies for next time!\n\n Wow, thank you for all the helpful information! I'm sure our listeners and their snails will be REALLY grateful to you!"
	}
	elseif Weather.Today == 5 //Electric
	{
		"\1\b[22]Ooh! My hair is standing up on end, look at that! There MUST be some electric energy building up in this area.\n\n \f[color,disable]Quick, get the batteries! Over here!\f[color,default]"
		"\1\b[22]Whoa! The studio lights are going HAYWIRE, hahaha! That's the POWER OF NATURE!\n\n Make sure you have emergency candles on hand, especially as we get into the evening and natural light starts to fade!"
		"\1\b[22]As a reminder, candles are the best option to have on hand as we get into the evening today! If you have a flashlight you MIGHT get lucky and get the batteries recharged for FREE today by the electronic interference. But your flashlight might ALSO get switched on without you realizing! There's nothing worse than finding out your flashlight's batteries died instead of getting recharged!\n\n The recommendation from experts is to remove batteries from all battery operated devices today, to avoid accidents that lead to battery drain!"
		"\1\b[22]Wow, I just felt a POWERFUL crackle behind me! And, gosh, look at that! My phone is COMPLETELY charged! What a miracle of nature!\n\n Hahaha, nothing beats the thrill of having electricity sparking all around you!"
		"\1\b[22]This just in: we've got word that all the lights in %(snailcity) suddenly started glowing incredibly bright, and then all the bulbs burst at once!\n\n Wow, they must have had a HUGE surge nearby. If you've been thinking about getting into the lightbulb business, now would be a great time!"
		"\1\b[22]I've been hearing news that some snails are having SUPERCHARGED races today thanks to the electric bursts overcharging their various electronic upgrades! If you're looking for a thrilling race, today is the day to head out to the track!"
		"\1\b[22]The weather today is ELECTRIFYING! Hahaha. It may be best to avoid electronics for the day, just in case they activate unexpectedly, or their batteries burst from becoming severely overcharged!\n\n Check our website on the snailernet for tips on how best to harness the electric jolts in the air and use them to your advantage!"
		
		//Dr. Power Watson
		"\1\b[22]Here on the show today we've got Dr.\![] Power Watson, an expert on this kind of electric weather, to give us the scoop on how these kinds of conditions come about. Dr.\![] Watson, why IS there stray electricity in the air on days like today?\n\n Well, this is a rather difficult weather phenomenon to study in detail, I'm sure you can understand.\n\n Oh, ABSOLUTELY! How do you study it when the electric bursts appear at random!?\n\n Haha, well, it's rather difficult! That's why right now, we've got a few competing theories as to what causes this phenomenon.\n\n Really!? Well, what's the most popular one at the moment?\n\n The leading theory right now is that these bursts of electricity are baby lightning bolts that haven't yet taken up refuge in a cloud. On their way up from the ground to the skies, sometimes they give us a bit of a shock!\n\n Oh... oh WOW! I hadn't expected it to be so... so adorable..."
		"\1\b[22]We've got a leading expert on electric weather here in the studio today, Dr.\![] Power Watson. Dr.\![] Watson, one of the questions we get a lot is how best to protect your electrical devices during a phenomenon like this?\n\n Well, the #1 thing to do is to remove batteries from your battery powered devices, as we all know. The second thing to do is to gather up all your battery powered devices, and keep them in your sight to see if they do anything strange!\n\n Oh, that's a good point! Even if you take the battery out of a flashlight, that doesn't mean it can't turn on anyway!\n\n Exactly. Beyond this, we also recommend unplugging as many non-essential corded appliances as you can, and make sure that any heat-generating devices are not in a position where they may pose a fire hazard.\n\n Ooh... ooh, I hope I remembered to move my space heater before I came to work today! Hahaha..."
		"\1\b[22]Dr.\![] Power Watson is with us here in the studio today to discuss electric weather, and various precautions we should all take. Dr.\![] Watson, our listeners want to know, what's the best thing to do for personal protection? What if you get a nasty shock?\n\n It's very unlikely that anyone will get a bad shock. Most shocks you will experience today are about as powerful as a minor static electricity shock.\n\n Haha, yeah, that matches my experience for sure!\n\n Still, it's best to be prepared. Our best advice is to wear long sleeves, and a simple metal bracelet on each arm. That will help to draw the electricity away from your body.\n\n Right, that makes sense! Thank you doctor!" //No it doesn't??? no it doesn't lol
	}
	elseif Weather.Today == 6 //Psionic storm
	{
		"\1\b[22]Today's psionic storm has been INTENSE! If you're experiencing symptoms, we encourage you to report them on our website on the snailernet.\n\n Describe your symtoms in AS MUCH detail as possible. Every report helps us understand this strange phenomenon a little more!"
		"\1\b[22]Be sure to keep an eye on your surroundings today! In general, it's considered safe to stay inside your home during a psionic storm, but there's ALWAYS the possibility that a slug may have snuck in without your knowledge! If you start feeling symptoms, get your tinfoil hat on and start searching for intruders! Stay safe out there!"
		"\1\b[22]Are YOU prepared to protect your mind when you head out today? If you don't have a tinfoil hat at the ready to deflect psionic beams, then check our website on the snailernet for tips on how to create your own!\n\n If your snails are going out with you, be sure to make hats for them, too! Staying safe is important on a day like today."
		"\1\b[22]We're getting lots of reports of psionic activity in %(snailcity)! There must be a TON of slugs gathered there, so be careful if you're headed there today!\n\n As always, if you start experiencing symptoms yourself, you're encouraged to report them on our website on the snailernet no matter where you're located! Your report will help us inform others of the hotspots of slug activity today!"
		"\1\b[22]Ooh, %(tinglingdownmyspine)! There must be a slug %(peeringinthewindows) again!\n\n \w8\w8\f[color,disable]Where's my tinfoil hat!?\f[color,default]"
		
		"\1\b[22]One of our listeners in %(snailcity) has reported %(feelingtinglysensations). That's a new one to me! These slugs are INVENTIVE, they've always got new ways to push our neural buttons!\n\n If you've been experiencing odd symptoms today, be sure to send us in a report so we can keep track of the spread and intensity of this phenomenon!"
		"\1\b[22]Are YOU being targetted by a slug's psionic attacks today!? Know the signs! Sufferers commonly report tingling sensations, headaches, and a feeling of being watched.\n\n If you exhibit these symptoms or anything else strange today, know that you're not alone! Our experts recommend staying at home and finding some sort of protection for your brain. The easiest solution is to make a hat out of tinfoil, but in a pinch, a metal bucket will do just fine to get you through the day!"
		"\1\b[22]Be on your guard today, slugs are EVERYWHERE, and their psionic powers are ultra-enhanced in these conditions! Protect your brain, and your snails' brains too!"
		"\1\b[22]Word is coming in that %(snailcity) is RIGHT at the center of a PSIONIC NEXUS today! Officials have issued a public safety warning, urging residents to stay at home until after the sun has gone down.\n\n It's intense stuff! I've heard reports of people dancing in the street, listening to music super loud, and even TALKING on the PHONE as they walk from place to place!"
		
		//Dr. Brianna Winters
		"\1\b[22]We've got an expert on the show today, Dr.\![] Brianna Winters, to tell us more about psionic storms and what causes this strange weather phenomenon! Dr.\![] Winters, what exactly is it about the conditions today that amplifies the psionic powers of slugs so drastically!?\n\n Well, that's just the thing. There is no extreme weather phenomenon today.\n\n ... You mean, slugs have this kind of power all the time, and they just hide it from us!?\n\n No, no, it's not that at all. I mean to say that there are no ""psionic powers"" at all. This is an ordinary day with fair weather, nothing unusual about it.\n\n But doctor, we have clear reports cropping up all over the place of people experiencing strange sensations today! You can't deny such clear evidence, can you!?\n\n I am not denying that people may be feeling something today, however, the science shows that those feelings are most likely to be caused by the nocebo effect and confirmation bias. After all, if you tell your listeners that they might feel something strange today, then their brains may genuinely generate strange feelings. This would lead them to believe that your reporting was correct, and something strange is happening, so they report their findings back to you... and it becomes a cycle where everyone feels more and more convinced it is real, even though there is no true cause outside of your own brain.\n\n ...\n\n ...\n\n %(snailpic) ...\n\n \w8\w8\w8\w8Well! Unfortunately, that's all the time we have for this portion of the show! It was nice meeting you, Dr.\![] Winters!\n\n Wait, but I've not had a chance to explain the%(emdash)!"
	}
	
	
	//Temps
	_citynum = RAND(ARRAYSIZE(CityTemps))
	_city = SnailCities[_citynum]
	_temp = TodaysTemp(_citynum)
	_temphigh = _temp + (TodaysSeed % 7) + 1 //yes this will be the same for all cities compared this day don't @ me lol
	_templow = _temp - (TodaysSeed % 6) - 1 //here too
	if _temphigh == 70 - 1; _temphigh = 70 // :)
	if _templow == 68 + 1; _templow = 68
	"\1\b[22]And we've got record-setting temperatures over in %(_city), for the first time this week they'll be reaching at least %(_temp)°F, with some estimates saying they might reach as high as %(_temphigh)°F!\n\n Wow, just wow. If they keep going this way, they might just reach their combined temperature goal of the week sooner than expected!"
	"\1\b[22]Today over in %(_city) you can expect temperatures of %(_temp)°F all through the afternoon, WITH the possibility of up to %(_temphigh)°F!\n\n As we all know, more degrees is better,%(br)so lets hope it keeps climbing!"
	"\1\b[22]Now let's have a look at %(_city). Today in %(_city) you can expect lows of %(_templow)°F, and highs of up to %(_temphigh)°F. But we're predicting that the average temperature will be right around %(_temp)°F all through the afternoon and going into the evening!"
	"\1\b[22]And now for the temperatures over in %(_city). Looks like we'll be seeing a nice steady %(_temp)°F throughout the afternoon, with lows predicted at %(_templow)°F, and highs at %(_temphigh)°F.\n\n I don't know about you, but those numbers all sound great to me! Isn't the weather awesome!?"
	"\1\b[22]Now, here's something astonishing; the temperature report for %(_city) has just come in, and the expected lows are %(_temphigh)°F, while the expected highs are %(_templow)°F! What an incredible first in nature, right!?\n\n ... What's that? ... OH! Hahaha, my numbers are backwards, sorry about that!\n\n The temperatures in %(_city) today are expected to be %(_temp)°F throughout the afternoon, with lows of %(_templow)°F, and highs of %(_temphigh)°F. That's more like it!"
	
	//Traffic
	//%(TrafficCity) is the function to use for a city name (avoids duplicates but CANNOT be displayed more than once per dialogue), %(StreetName) for random street name
	"\1\b[22]NOW over to Tailgating Terror with a traffic update. Tailgate, how's those %(TrafficCity) streets looking today?\n\n %(snailpic) Bad.\n\n Yikes, we hate to see it! Thanks for the update, now back to the weather!"
	"\1\b[22]Time for another traffic update, lets check in with our lovely Tailgating Terror in %(TrafficCity)! Tailgate, how's it looking over at %(StreetName)?\n\n %(snailpic) %(ANY('Clogged,Crash,Pileup,Honk,Horns,Brakes,Gridlock,Chaos')).\n\n Ouch, I sure hope none of our listeners are stuck in that mess! Now for next week's forecast!"
	"\1\b[22]It's time to shake things up a bit!%(br)We've asked our traffic expert, Tailgating Terror, to have a look at %(StreetName), %(StreetName), and %(StreetName) over in %(TrafficCity), and to give us a summary of the situation there. Tailgate, how's it looking!?\n\n %(snailpic) Slow.\n\n You heard it here first, folks! THAT'S the \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] advantage!"
	"\1\b[22]Next up, we've got a traffic report from our snail on the ground, Tailgating Terror, who is over in %(TrafficCity). Tailgate, how's it looking down at %(StreetName)?\n\n %(snailpic) %(ANY('Empty,Clear,Nothing')).\n\n Wow, what a surprise! How about %(StreetName)?\n\n %(snailpic) Same.\n\n Amazing! If you're looking for a good ol' fashioned street race, sounds like that's the place to be!"
	_streetname = StreetName
	"\1\b[22]And now for another look at the traffic, this time over in %(TrafficCity)! Our snail on the ground, Tailgating Terror, has just radioed in with the latest report. Tailgate, give us the scoop on %(_streetname)!\n\n %(snailpic) %(ANY('Fast,Speeding,Race,Vroom')).\n\n Awesome! If you like to race, get yourself over to %(_streetname) as soon as possible before it gets choked up!"
	
	
	//Predictions
	if Weather.Today == Weather.Tomorrow
	{
		_thatsunnyweather = ("those sunny skies","the protection from the clouds","the hydrating downpour","watching the worm migration","this breezy, sneezy weather","that extra energized air","the benefits of the ongoing psionic storm")[Weather.Today]
		"\1\b[22]If you've been enjoying %(_thatsunnyweather) today, then you're in luck because it'll be continuing just the same tomorrow!\n\n Forecasts are calling for the current weather patterns to hold for the next 24 hours at least, and if you stay tuned we'll keep giving YOU all the latest weather information on the #1 weather source you can trust, \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default]."
		
		_sunnyweather = ("sunny weather","cloudy skies","rainfall","worminess","sneezy weather","electric bursts","psionic interference")[Weather.Today]
		"\1\b[22]All our forecasts today show that the current weather patterns will hold, so tomorrow you can expect to see the same %(_sunnyweather) that we're having today. If you're traveling, make sure that you're factoring in how that may affect your route!\n\n Whether you're on the road or staying at home, stay tuned, and we'll keep YOU updated on where the weather is going next here at \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default]."
		
		_sunnyskies = ("sunny skies","cloudy days","rain showers","to watch the worm migrations","breezy days and you don't have allergies","having the dead batteries in your drawer suddenly recharge themselves","feeling the tingles from the potential psionic energy in the air")[Weather.Today]
		_thatsunis = ("that sun is","those clouds are","these showers are","the worm migration is","these high winds are","the high levels of electricity in the air are","this psionic storm shows no signs of stopping and is")[Weather.Today]
		_stockupon = ("regularly apply sunscreen","get out while they can and enjoy the cooler weather","wear rain boots and keep an eye on their snails","watch where they step; you never know where those worms might get to","get out their battery testers, and make sure to have a spare radio just in case","watch what they're thinking today, and maybe consider picking up a special psychic energy-proof hat")[Weather.Today]
		"\1\b[22]Well, if you like %(_sunnyskies) then you're in luck, because %(_thatsunis) going to continue right into tomorrow. We're advising everyone to %(_stockupon)!\n\n Make sure to check back with us tomorrow, and we at \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] will keep YOU updated on whatever the weather has in store for us next!"
		
		_thatsunwill = ("That sun will continue beating down","There will be no breaks in the clouds","These storms are going to keep rolling in","The worm migration is predicted to continue","The extreme allergen levels we've been seeing will continue","The electrified atmosphere and jolting side effects will continue","The buildup of psychic energy has not yet dissipated and will be volatile")[Weather.Today]
		"\1\b[22]I hope you're all enjoying this weather, because we are LOCKED IN for the next day at least! %(_thatsunwill) all through tomorrow as well.\n\n Stay tuned to \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] and we'll give YOU updated weather predictions as soon as they become available!"
		
		"\1\b[22]Isn't this weather great!? I hope you're asking your friends the same question, because we're going to have the exact same %(_sunnyweather) tomorrow, too! Look forward to it, and for all the latest predictions, be SURE to tune in to \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default]!"
	}
	else //Changing
	{
		_weathery = ("sunny","cloudy","rainy","wormy","sneezy","electrified","psychically charged")[Weather.Today]
		_sunnyskies = ("sunny skies as far as the eye can see","clouds, clouds, and more clouds","wet and humid as storms come rolling through","the perfect conditions for the worm migration","a bad day for allergens, with sneezes and sniffles all around","powerfully electrifying","a day of high psychic energy")[Weather.Tomorrow]
		"\1\b[22]If you're hoping for a break from this %(_weathery) weather, you won't have to wait long!\n\n Mother nature will be shaking things up soon; we're predicting tomorrow will be %(_sunnyskies)! Stay tuned for further details after the break."
		
		_thissunnyweather = ("this sunny weather","this cloudy weather","this rainy weather","the worm migration","the intense burst of allergens in the air","the electrifying zip in the air","the psionic storm")[Weather.Today]
		_sunny = ("sunny","cloudy","rainy","wormy","sneezy","electric","tinfoil hat")[Weather.Today]
		_nothingbut = ("the hot sun beating down and warming everything up","puffy clouds all throughout the sky","rain, rain, RAIN","worms","pollen so strong it'll knock your socks off","free energy%(emdash) if you've got batteries to catch it in","terror as we all try to keep prying minds out of our thoughts")[Weather.Tomorrow]
		"\1\b[22]At long last, it looks like %(_thissunnyweather) is coming to an end! That's right, this chain of %(_sunny) days is coming to a close, and starting tomorrow you can look forward to nothing but %(_nothingbut)!"
		
		_brighthot = ("the bright hot sun with no clouds to protect us from its scorching rays","clouds scattered about, blanketing the sky","storms rolling in relentlessly","the worms migrating again","allergens everywhere, and sneezes to match","electrifying zaps that will fill every room with energy","a great mass of psychic energy that is sure to put everyone on edge")[Weather.Tomorrow]
		"\1\b[22]Woo, who's looking forward to something different tomorrow!? I sure am! Tomorrow we're supposed to see %(_brighthot)!\n\n Whatever the weather, Haley Storme is on the case! And I'll be sure to bring YOU all the latest details, so tune in tomorrow as we learn more!"
		
		_lotsofsun = ("lots of sun","cloudy skies","rain","worms","extreme allergy warnings","electrifying bursts of energy","a psionic storm")[Weather.Tomorrow]
		"\1\b[22]As a reminder, %(_thissunnyweather) won't last forever, and in fact tomorrow the forecasts are calling for %(_lotsofsun). So if you're an enthusiast, get out there and SOAK IT UP while you can!"
		
		"\1\b[22]It's a great day today for sure, but tomorrow there'll be even MORE weather! Current forecasts are calling for %(_lotsofsun), isn't that exciting!?\n\n I know I'll be looking forward to it! Be sure to stay tuned to \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] for all of the juicy details as soon as they become avaliable!"
	}
	
	//Misc
	_snailcity = snailcity
	_snailcity2 = snailcity
	while _snailcity == _snailcity2
	{
		_snailcity2 = snailcity
	}
	"\1\b[22]And now we're going to take a look at the temperatures over in%(emdash) whoa! Hahaha, %(besttoavoid(_snailcity))\n\n We'll come back around to %(_snailcity) once we've got our equipment functioning properly again. For now, let's move on to %(_snailcity2), where the temperatures look more reasonable!"
	"\1\b[22]This just in, I'm getting reports about a massive storm cloud brewing over %(_snailcity)! This might be a big one folks!\n\n \w8\w8... Oh, what's that? Hold on a moment, I'm getting new information that the cloud is actually just %(fromabbq(_snailcity))!\n\n False alarm, phew! But rest assured that if there WAS a sudden weather event, we at \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] would get you information as fast as it becomes available, and maybe even faster!"
	"\1\b[22]\![set,balloonwait,1.7]... Zzz... Temperatures today... Mmf...\![set,balloonwait,1.0]\n\n ... yyYAAAA%(emdash)! So cold!! ...\w8\w8\n\n Oh, we're-\w8\w8 \w8Th-\w8 This is HALEY STORME for \f[italic,1]FIRST PLACE FORECASTS\f[italic,default], and today is going to be FULL OF WEATHER!!\n\n CLOUDS, WIND, TEMPERATURE, YOU NAME IT AND WE'VE GOT IT TODAY!! ... Probably!!\n\n \w8\w8\f[color,disable]Where did my notes go? Are they under the desk...!? How did they get THERE...!\f[color,default]"
	"\1\b[22]If you think today's weather is great, wait until you see our forecasts for next week, where there's going to be even MORE weather!\n\n Ooh, I'm so excited about what mother nature has in store for us! The temperatures, the humidity levels, the wind speeds%(emdash) all coming soon!"
	
	_randforecast = WeekForecastIndex
	while _randforecast == WeekForecastIndex //Ensure no dupes
	{
		_randforecast = RAND(ARRAYSIZE(WeekForecast))
	}
	_oldweekforecast = WeekForecast[WeekForecastIndex][0,'|']
	_newweekforecast = WeekForecast[_randforecast][1,'|'] //Picks a new one but it is NOT assigned UNLESS the dialogue plays due to the raise tag
	"\![raise,OnUpdateWeekForecast,%(_randforecast)]\1\b[22]We've got an update for YOU on the forecast for this upcoming week. Our previous reports were calling for %(_oldweekforecast), but new data just in says that this week we're more likely to see %(_newweekforecast)!\n\n That's the weather for you! Stay tuned to \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default], and%(br)we'll keep you updated as more data comes in!"
	
	"\1\b[22]For those of you waiting on more details about the forecast for the upcoming week, just be patient a little longer! All our helper snails are busy crunching the numbers and running calculations, and we'll have the results in for you before you know it!\n\n While we wait, how about next we have a look at the temperatures we're expecting to see tonight?"
	"\1\b[22]And now for my favorite part of the hour, the \f[italic,1]First Place Forecast\f[italic,default] Temperature Stack%(tm)! Let's see how %(_city) stacks up!\n\n Our little helper snails have been working hard tallying up all the numbers, and the results are now in! %(_city)'s Temperature Stack%(tm) for today is... %(_temp + _temphigh + _templow)%(degrees)F!\n\n Wow! Just look at those numbers soar! It's not quite a record, but it's getting close! You can do it, %(_city)!!\n\n However they calculate these numbers is a mystery to me, but I'm assured that it's a very rigorous and scientific process that accurately represents each region. So have no worry! We'll keep bringing YOU the latest Temperature Stack%(tm) data, 100% guaranteed to be accurate and correct,%(br)just as we always have!"
	"\1\b[22]We've got a special segment today! We've brought in renowned meteorologist Dr.\![] Sunnie Day to set the record straight on one of the greatest mysteries in weather!\n\n Well, I'm delighted to be here.\n\n Dr.\![] Day, I have just one question for you. No weaseling out of it now that you're here!\n\n Oh, well I certainly wouldn't want to%(emdash)\n\n Dr.\![] Day, what is the small circle symbol that appears every time we talk about the temperature!?\n\n ... I beg your pardon?\n\n Look, here, where it says %(RAND(20) + 70)%(degrees)F!\n\n The... degrees symbol?\n\n A-ha! So it does have a name! Why does it appear across all of our data, even going back into our oldest archives!?\n\n I'm... rather astonished at the question. It's because it is%(emdash)\n\n OOOH! Is it a snail mark!? I bet it's a snail mark! That would make sense with how many helper snails we have in the studio!\n\n ...\n\n Wait, Dr.\![] Day, where are you going! \w8\w8...%(br)Well! That's the end of this segment, I hope that burning question has now been answered for all our listeners! Now, how about we have a look at the hourly forecast, armed with our new knowledge..." //TODO this could be on TodaysChoices if i came up with more lol | possible new one: asking a different doctor why clouds look green from above... you know, like on radar view
	"\1\b[22]If you're looking for a way to engage more with the weather, why not try our new \f[italic,1]Which Weather Phenomenon Are You\f[italic,default] quiz on our website? It's totally free, and TOTALLY AWESOME!\n\n I tried it myself, and my result said that I'm most likely to be a tornado! Hahaha, imagine that! And YOU can try it now, for FREE, and see how you compare to me!"
	"\1\b[22]Sometimes our listeners ask me if the day's weather is suitable to head outside in. But I always say the same thing: ANY weather is suitable if you're brave enough! Get out there and experience the weather with your WHOLE BODY!\n\n \w8\w8Next up, our experts are speculating that there might be %(acalamity) in a few weeks, so we've brought one of them on to discuss what kinds of preparation we should all begin doing..."
	
	"\1\b[22]Are YOU prepared in case of extreme weather? To help you find out, we've made a handy list of steps you can take!\n\n 1.\![] Make sure you have a backup supply of water. You never know when you might be out of the house for long periods of time, and hydration is key!\n\n 2.\![] ALWAYS have a box of extreme weather supplies in your car, in case the weather changes while you're away from home! Don't be caught unaware!\n\n 3.\![] Bring extra batteries and storage media for your equipment! Whether you're photographing weather events, taking video, recording sounds, WHATEVER the case may be, you'll want to make sure you've always got plenty of power and storage space!\n\n 4.\![] Make sure your friends know your plans for various weather conditions! Where will you all head? Who's bringing snacks, who's bringing supplies like towels and sunscreen, and who's covering the camera? Knowing what everyone's role will be is crucial to properly experiencing a major weather event!"
	"\1\b[22]We're going to take a break in a moment to hear a message from our sponsors. But before that, a \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] Cool Weather Fact%(tm)!\n\n Did you know that %(theresweathereverywhere)!? How's that for amazing!"
	"\1\b[22]Rain or shine, %(ANY('worms or no,clouds or snow')), \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] is your #1 destination for EVERYTHING weather, and even some things that aren't!"
	"\1\b[22]Do YOU or someone you know REALLY know the weather? Why not put your skills to the test with our online weather prediction survey!\n\n Simply visit our website on the snailernet, and enter in your own personal forecast. In a week, we'll see how accurate you were!\n\n If your skills are TRULY top notch, you might just get a job offer then and there! That's the kind of opportunity you can't pass up, am I right!?"
	"\1\b[22]There's going to be a slight delay on the temperature data for this next hour, folks. It sounds like someone in the break room dropped their sandwich, causing all the lettuce to spill out of it, and, well. Let's just say our helper snails are taking a long lunch break today! Hahaha.\n\n Sorry for any inconvenience, but while we wait, why don't I read out the data from last hour again!"
	
	"\1\b[22]I'm SO pumped to tell you all about the latest forecast data, and that's COMING UP SOON!\n\n ... But, my producer is telling me that I have to finish the traffic report before we can do that, eheheh... So, let's have a look over at how things are moving in %(TrafficCity)!"
	"\1\b[22]Later this evening we're going to have an expert on to tell us about the internal anatomy of clouds! I hope%(br)you're excited, because I sure am!\n\n Wow, what kind of inner secrets do you think clouds have!? We'll find out tonight with Dr. McLeod!"
	"\1\b[22]Don't forget folks, next week we're going to be looking at the \f[italic,1]First Place Forecasts\f[italic,default] Yearly Temperature Tracker%(tm) and checking on our progress so far this year!\n\n All the highest temperature readings from every day so far will be added up,%(br)and we'll see how high those numbers soar! It's gonna be SO much fun to see where we're at!\n\n If you'd like to participate and help us bump the numbers up by a few more degrees, don't forget our #1 tip: get yourself a space heater, put it outside, and let it do its thing. It's THE most simple and effective way to make an impact!"
	
	switch WeeksLettuceHarvestIndex
	{
		"\1\b[22]The lettuce report is IN, and the lettuce crops this season are steady and reliable, just as you'd expect from such a critical operation! There should be plenty of lettuce for every snail, and more besides. Look forward to it hitting the shelves soon!"
		"\1\b[22]I'm looking over the lettuce report for this season, and we have got a BUMPER crop to look forward to this year! All the conditions have come together just right to produce lots of sweet lettuce which is sure to bring a smile to snails everywhere!\n\n With all this surplus, it's sure to bring the price of lettuce down, so be sure to get out there and eat a lot of it to keep our currency stable, hahaha!"
		"\1\b[22]An unfortunate turn of events, the lettuce reports for this season are looking a little scary! It seems like the yields this year were tasty%(emdash) for the local bugs, BEFORE they even reached harvest!\n\n That means we might be a little short on lettuce this season, so you might consider introducing your snail to some other leafy greens, like spinach or kale. It may take some time to adjust, but it's good to acquire the taste in case of shortages!"
		"\1\b[22]Shocking news this season as we look at the lettuce report%(emdash) we have record numbers, but not the record you'd hope! It seems like almost everyone switched to planting cabbage this year!?\n\n Officials are recommending that dietary lettuce be reduced to a minimum to keep the value of our currency stable, and that we all switch to eating cabbage for the time being.\n\n I don't know about you, but dinner time just isn't going to be the same without a head of lettuce to pick through! And the thought of sandwiches with shredded CABBAGE!? That sounds like a crime!"
		"\1\b[22]We're just getting word in that there is an EXTREME lettuce surplus at the lettuce farms right now, more lettuce than you can even imagine. I guess the weather's been perfect for it!\n\n Reports say that we're going to have a period of massive inflation, followed by massive deflation as the farmer's market corrects itself next season. Mandates for every citizen to consume at least one head of lettuce per day to help control the spike are under consideration, and I don't know about you all, but I am ALREADY surpassing that in my daily routine!\n\n In fact, here's a challenge for you: if you already consume at least one head of lettuce per day, consider doubling it to TWO heads of lettuce per day until this season of abundance is over! Eat delicious food, show off to all your friends, AND help the world's economy stay stable!"
	}
	
	switch WeeksSnailHarvestIndex
	{
		"\1\b[22]We've gotten word in from our local snail farms, and it's sounding like the next batch of racing snails is something really amazing! I'm told that the class about to graduate from snail school has all gotten straight S's!\n\n If you're looking to take on a new snail,%(br)or even become a first-time sponsor, NOW is the time to do it! Get those snails while you can, because this batch is sure to be snatched up quick, and there are CERTAIN to be some history-makers in there!"
		"\1\b[22]This just in, we've gotten a look at the latest batch of racer snails from the local snail farms, and let me tell you, they do NOT seem like winners. They've got no energy to them! Several of them reportedly flunked out of snail school, and the ones that are graduating have only barely managed to get a passing grade.\n\n Well, I only have one thing to say to those snails: struggling with snail school DOESN'T define you! Who knows, maybe one day you'll find a great opportunity as a weather presenter! So keep those tentacles up, and GIVE IT YOUR ALL!"
		"\1\b[22]Shocking news from the snail farms: the most recent batch of graduating snails has been given their racer names, and EVERY single one was non-alliterative!\n\n Word has it that chaos broke out as the name wheel picked non-alliterative combinations over and OVER. Experts are saying that the chances such a thing could occur given the number of snails in that class are a measly%(br)0.0000000002%! That's SO many zeroes!"
		"\1\b[22]We got a notice in from one of the local snail farms that a batch of young snails has ESCAPED the farm and is now out on the loose! Locals are being encouraged to watch where they step, and if they spot any snails, particularly ones that aren't quite mature yet, to catch them and check the top of their shells for a dot of UV-reactive paint that the farm uses to track wayward snails.\n\n If you've found an escaped snail, you're encouraged to return it back to the farm as soon as possible. These snails haven't finished snail school yet, and are still vulnerable out in the world at large! With any luck, we'll be able to recover most of them, and classes can resume!"
		"\1\b[22]In an unprecedented turn of events, snail production this season was severely limited by various issues plaguing the local farms, and as a result there is an EXTREME snail shortage right now. One of my sources said that it's so bad, some farms have been recruiting slugs and giving them FAKE SHELLS so they can get into snail school and learn to race, to try and meet demand!\n\n If you sponsor a snail and find that it doesn't seem thrilled about alliteration or that it moves around like it's not used to having a shell, that might be why! Experts are saying that if you plan to sponsor a new snail within the next several months, you should bring a magnifying glass to inspect its shell closely. It's better to be safe than sorry!"
	}
}

//Bill Carde & Blanca Chek
//Turbo Trends
RadioStation.Shopping : nonoverlap_pool
{
	//"\1\b[20]wow these deals sure are hot!"
	"\1\b[22]Next up we've got the Radio Antenna! You're a bit of an expert on this item, aren't you, Blanca?\n\n I'd like to think so, Bill! The Radio Antenna has a clean, sleek look that's sure to go with any snail, while offering the convenience of a standard radio anywhere you go! What could be cooler than listening to us here at \f[italic,1]Turbo Trends\f[italic,default] while gardening, cleaning, exercising, or even during a trip to the mall?\n\n And for the low price of only %(LL(90)), I don't think it gets any better than this!"
	"\1\b[22]And now for a personal favorite of mine, the BIG ROCKET!\n\n Oh, Bill, this one again?\n\n Yes indeed, Blanca! When it comes to sheer speed, it's hard to beat the numbers you'll get from strapping a giant jet engine to your shell!\n\n That's true, although it's not the most elegant. And the risks%(emdash)\n\n %(emdash)Are outweighed in many cases by the rewards! Sure, the loss of control makes it far more likely you'll crash, but isn't that what helmets are for!?\n\n Well, yes, a helmet will protect your head. But it's so... \f[italic,1]garish\f[italic,default] of a solution. Surely there are ways to increase your speed that aren't so drastic...?\n\n Nonsense! If you want big numbers, the best value for your leaf is the BIG ROCKET! Get one today and watch your snails fly!"
	"\1\b[22]Well, what have you got for us next, Blanca?\n\n I'd like to tell you about our new lineup of trucker hats! They come in an assortment of colors, and they cost just %(LL(100)) each.\n\n Now Blanca, we get this question quite regularly; why is it that these hats have brims? Isn't it a bit silly since a snail's eyes are perched higher than any shade afforded by the brim?\n\n That's true, Bill! But the fact of the matter is that a trucker hat simply wouldn't be a trucker hat without that big brim!\n\n You make an excellent point, it just wouldn't be the same. And who doesn't want to be able to match with their snail?\n\n Exactly! Now, let me tell you about the new designs we have this year. We've got a nice orange trucker hat with a design featuring an orange, and a lovely green trucker hat with an adorable leaf!\n\n What a great lineup we have! No matter your snail's aesthetic, you're sure to be able to find one that fits. And for a very affordable price!"
	"\1\b[22]Bill, you said you wanted to talk about one of your favorite economy options next?\n\n Yes, indeed I do! Some of the best speed options can be pretty pricey, but we've got a great piece that will get you a little more 'oomph' without breaking the bank!\n\n Oh, do tell?\n\n Have a look at this box fan! You can strap this right to the shell of your snail, and the breeze it generates will give you that extra edge that you need in a pinch.\n\n Ooh, well, that may be true, but I think any style critic worth their salt would agree that it's simply an eyesore to look at. If you're hoping to be cool, you'd be well advised to stay away from this one.\n\n So you say, Blanca, but consider this: what is the purpose of a fan if not to make you cool!\n\n I... Ooh, now that's just not right. But all the same I can't argue that point, so I suppose it should be called a net neutral as far as coolness goes.\n\n That's right! A little boost of speed without losing any coolness, and it only costs a mere %(LL(150))! What a deal!"
	"\1\b[22]Now have a look at these: a brand new set of tires!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Ooh, aah!\f[italic,default]\n\n Blanca, do you know what's great about these tires?\n\n Let me guess Bill, these are those new racing tires you've been talking about that grip the track better and increase your speed?\n\n That's right! But not only that, having a set of tires for your snail will help to keep it upright so it doesn't topple over, reducing the risk of a crash!\n\n That's true! And nobody could argue that a slick set of tires isn't cool. This is an all-around benefit and a no-brainer for any snail loadout." //TODO if the tires get colors I want to add comments about it here
	
	"\1\b[22]And over here, we've got our fine selection of round glasses in a variety of colors! Guaranteed to give your snail perfect 20/20 vision, no matter what the current condition of its eyes may be.\n\n Ooh, now Bill, explain to me how it is that these glasses improve your speed?\n\n Well Blanca, it all comes down to this: the better your sight, the better you can see obstacles in the road to avoid them. Not only that, clear vision means you can be confident that there are no obstacles in your path, allowing you to rush forward and give it your all!\n\n That does make sense, I suppose. And it also explains why your snails are less likely to crash and explode while wearing them.\n\n Very much the truth, although I think the bigger factor there is that the glasses allow you to read the warning labels on various equipment!\n\n Oh, that's true... \f[color,disable]Is that a major issue?%(br)Should we be reading out the warnings on the show...?\f[color,default]\n\n The best part about glasses, though, is that you can always stack them up! More glasses means better vision, which means greater confidence on the track! If you think 20/20 vision is good, wait until you see how great%(br)40/40 or 60/60 is!\n\n I... well, maybe, but at a price of%(br)%(LL(2020)) for each pair that's going to add up quick and really hurt your wallet! Not to mention, these glasses have sort of a ""nerd"" reputation, and I think stacking multiple pairs might just amplify that effect beyond what's acceptable..."
	"\1\b[22]And this is your daily reminder that racing stripes are an easy and cost-effective way to improve your snail's performance!\n\n It's true, Bill. Racing stripes never go out of style, and they look great on just about any snail! They pair well with all sorts of shell paints and patterns, and can really tie a look together.\n\n Indeed! Not only that, each stripe you add to your snail gives it a little boost in speed, which might be just enough to reach that next spot on the leaderboards!\n\n Well, now how does that work? Aren't stripes a style choice?\n\n Yes they are, Blanca. But as they say,%(br)""A snail that feels like a racecar will race like a racecar""!\n\n Oh, how wonderful. And at a mere%(br)%(LL(100)) for a pair, that's just %(LL(50)) per stripe, which I think we can all agree is a fabulous deal."
	"\1\b[22]Next, I'd like to talk about the various accessories we have that allow your snail to carry more items, completely hands-free! We have a lovely sling bag that can fit easily onto any snail, or if you need something bigger, this hefty saddle bag!\n\n You were very excited about these before we went on the air today, Blanca. What more can you tell us about them?\n\n Well, just look at them. They feature sturdy double-stitched designs which don't sacrifice style for utility. Any snail wearing one of these well-crafted bags is sure to catch some eyes. And best of all, they're made of 100% genuine pleather!\n\n Well, now, that all seems well and good, but they don't look very aerodynamic...\n\n It's true, you'll have to give up a bit of speed for these. But I think it's worthwhile; snails can hold so much more lettuce at once with a bag like this, and we all know that lettuce-laden snails are happy snails! And that's before you consider that they may like to keep other favored items in their bags, like twigs or small pebbles.\n\n I can certainly see that happening, but imagine the added weight...! If you want to have the fastest snail on the track, this is surely not the way to go."
	"\1\b[22]Next in our program today is this wonderful lineup of helmets! Bill, why don't you explain the benefits of a helmet to our listeners?\n\n Well, Blanca, that is... er... They sure are good at being helmets!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Huh? What?\f[italic,default]\n\n Haha, yes. Helmets! They're great. They're... well. They're head protection, that's important! Depending on what you prioritize!\n\n It's true, Blanca. They won't give you any additional speed, but if you have a lot of speed-increasing items, you've likely got a decent chance to crash, so... Maybe you should consider investing?\n\n Ooh, but be prepared to take a hit when it comes to style, unfortunately. Boldness is important when it comes to style, and a helmet... sort of communicates that... \w8\w8\f[color,disable]I'm not sure I can say that on the radio. Bill, what other features do these helmets have?\f[color,default]\n\n \f[color,disable]I don't know! Is there a script around here we can read off of? Anyone?\f[color,default]\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Uhh? Uwuh?\f[italic,default]\n\n \f[color,disable]This is taking too long. Think, Blanca, think... \f[color,default] Er... Well, these helmets come in a wide variety of colors, all made of the finest quality plastic! I'm sure you and your snail can find a color you like.\n\n We currently have a large stock of all the colors, so get your favorites now before these start selling out! \f[color,disable]Haha...\f[color,default]"
	"\1\b[22]When it comes to the ultimate upgrades in both speed and style, I think there's one undeniable winner: Wings!\n\n I have to agree, Blanca. Wings really are the perfect outfit, with a sleek form factor that fits any style, and unparalleled aerodynamics that will propel your snail to victory. There's a reason that the design is coveted even though birds are a snail's natural predator!\n\n It's true! And if bird wings aren't for you, there are also bat wings that trade off a bit of that speed for a sharper, cooler aesthetic that is sure to win you extra style points.\n\n That being said, both styles of wings are available in a wide variety of colors! No matter your aesthetic goals, I'm sure you can find just the right pair of wings to suit your snail.\n\n Ooh, but be careful! Wings are expensive! For very good reason, of course. They provide incredible benefits with no notable downside. No notable downside besides breaking the bank, that is!\n\n Hahaha! Indeed, that's very true. Shop around and make sure you know what you want before you buy! And if you've got any coupons, this would be a good time to use them."
	
	"\1\b[22]Ooh, Bill, have you heard about the trendy new style going around?\n\n No, Blanca, I haven't. What's new in your world?\n\n Moonwalking! For a fee, a snail can be taught how to race while facing backwards!\n\n I... well, I would never have expected that. Surely that would be much slower than racing the normal way? Not to mention it must be incredibly dangerous.\n\n Well, yes, that's true. But the flair! The drama! Snails daring enough to race in reverse might be the coolest thing I've ever seen!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Woo! Yay!\f[italic,default]\n\n ... Well, I'd sure be impressed if they managed to complete a race that way, I suppose!" //TODO if we change the name from moonwalking, change this
	"\1\b[22]You all know it and love it, it's THE icon of style. The poster child, the item everyone thinks of when they hear ""cool""! That's right, it's... a slick pair of shades!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Oooh!\f[italic,default]\n\n This certainly is a popular item, Blanca. Why don't you tell us a bit about why?\n\n Well, Bill, I think they speak for themselves. One need only gaze upon them once to understand why they are THE pinnacle of fashion! I'm no fortune teller, but I can't imagine any possible future where they would fall out of style.\n\n Perhaps so, but they really are all looks and no utility, aren't they? I've heard of racers getting into crashes because the darkened lenses make it harder for them to see obstacles on the track. That seems like a pretty big concern to me.\n\n It's true, they can have that effect. But it's a tradeoff! A little risk for great reward. Isn't that what you say for some of your favorite speed-enhancing items that make snails go so fast they can lose control?\n\n I%(emdash) \w8\w8Haha, well, you've got me there! I suppose I do say that. But with speed the loss of control is inevitable, I always figured that with style you could sidestep that issue.\n\n Nonsense! The coolest snails are the ones that are bold, daring, and take risks in the name of great taste. If there's no risk involved, then it simply isn't very cool!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Yeah! Yay!\f[italic,default]"
	"\1\b[22]Here's one to help you beat that summer heat, it's a selection of sun hats! These wide, floppy brims will keep the sun off of your snail, helping it to stay cool and moist even when the sun is hot!\n\n That's a good idea, Blanca. We all know that when snails get too warm in the summer, they tend to want to go into estivation. And that's not good for their racing careers!\n\n Indeed it's not, Bill! I would encourage every sponsor out there to pick up some sun hats for their snails, it's much better to get one early before estivation becomes a problem. They come in a variety of colors, too, so you can pick something cute to match your snail's look!"
	"\1\b[22]And now for something a little mysterious and magical. It's this lovely witch hat!\n\n Oh, now that certainly is a bold aesthetic piece, Blanca.\n\n Yes, Bill, it is! Front and center in your snail's outfit, and with that unmistakable shape and color, it's hard to miss. A lot of folks pass it up because it's such a powerful look, but I think any snail confident enough to wear it day-to-day would be the envy of all its peers, even if they won't admit it!\n\n I think I'd be envious myself, haha!"
	"\1\b[22]Next up is... uh. Well. Next up is this... cigarette!\n\n ...\n\n ... \f[color,disable]Say something, Bill!\f[color,default]\n\n \f[color,disable]What am I supposed to say, it has nothing to do with speed!\f[color,default]\n\n \f[color,disable]Ooh... \f[color,default]Ahem. Well, it's... You see, the cigarette is one of the coolest styles you can have! It, er...\n\n Blanca, are you alright?\n\n Ooh, I just can't do it Bill! I'm putting my job here at risk, but I just can't bear to see so many little snails hurt themselves trying to be cool! Cigarettes are dangerous and I won't endorse them.\n\n It's true, how many snails have you seen go up in flames on the starting line? These things are a trap! I don't know how something so volatile has gotten onto the market in the first place.\n\n \f[color,disable]Bill, maybe it's time to move on.\f[color,default]\n\n \f[color,disable]Yes, let's...\f[color,default]"
	
	_snailname = SnailNameGenerator(,'alliteration')
	"\1\b[22]Next up we have this pair of goggles! Good for protecting your snail's eyes from the wind or debris.\n\n Well, that seems like a strange one for your list, doesn't it, Blanca?\n\n Whatever do you mean, Bill?\n\n It's just that items geared towards speed and physical advantages are usually the ones I talk about!\n\n Oh, Bill, these are FASHION goggles! Just look at how they fit on our dear %(_snailname).\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Gubbo!\f[italic,default]\n\n ... I'm not sure that%(emdash)\n\n They're the coolest goggles in town! They're not lab goggles or nerd goggles or whatever else one might think, they're made to enhance your charm factor.\n\n And protect from wind and debris?\n\n Everyone looks great in goggles, and your snail will too!" //TODO idk why i feel like these snails... don't speak in real words lol?????? i'm attached to "gubbo"... but also like....................... they should either talk in snail lang or english lol
	"\1\b[22]Next up on my list, I'd like to talk about this great Hot Rod Exhaust.\n\n Ooh, now that's certainly an eye-catcher!\n\n Yes indeed! That shiny chrome body is sure to turn some heads, but it's not just for style, this serves an important function too!\n\n Oh, do tell?\n\n Engines produce a lot of heat and toxic fumes! If you want to race faster, it's important to vent both of those things away, and that's just what this Hot Rod Exhaust will do for you.\n\n I see! It sounds like an important upgrade. And unbelievably, they've made a necessary item fashionable as well! It's not every day you see something that hits both of those criteria.\n\n It certainly isn't! Our listeners would be wise to invest in one of these, no matter their racing strategy." //TODO names ???
	"\1\b[22]How about this high grade shell polish by Shell Shiners? If you want to make that shell sparkle and shine, Shell Shiners is the choice for you!\n\n That's right, Bill! Every snail deserves a shiny shell so they can look their very best. And I've found Shell Shiners shell polish to be one of the highest quality products on the market.\n\n You really need a fine grit to get that perfect glossy sheen, and Shell Shiners produces the finest grit polishes you can get. Buy some today, and if you're not happy with your purchase they offer a 90 day money-back guarantee!"
	"\1\b[22]Bill, have you heard about the new paints that %(TodaysChoice(chromecolors)) released just this week?\n\n No I haven't, Blanca. Why don't you tell us all about them?\n\n I sure will! The new lineup of %(TodaysChoice(chromecolors)) paints offer all the same vibrancy and depth as their existing paints, but with %(TodaysChoice(betterrustprotection))!\n\n Wow, %(TodaysChoice(betterrustprotection))? Now that sounds like a deal to me! I better head out to the store once we're done here and get some right away.\n\n That's right, if you want to stay on the cutting edge of style, the new paints from %(TodaysChoice(chromecolors)) are a must!"
	"\1\b[22]And here comes %(_snailname) with our next item!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Ubuh! \w8Uhh?\f[italic,default] \w8\f[italic,1]\f[color,disable]Crash!\f[color,default]\f[italic,default]\n\n Oh no! %(_snailname), are you alright!?\n\n %(snailpic) \f[color,disable]\f[italic,1]Ohhhhh... Owie...\f[italic,default]\f[color,default]\n\n Looks like we'll have to wait on that one, folks! Not to worry, %(_snailname) just had a bit of a tumble, but it'll be alright in a moment. In the meantime, how about we have a look at this %(newsetofwheels) that was just released?"
	
	_aquaticthemed = SPLIT(aquaticthemed,"|")
	_stickystickers = SPLIT(stickystickers,"|")
	"\1\b[22]Now for something sure to delight any snail: a new pack of %(_aquaticthemed[0]) stickers from %(_stickystickers[0])!\n\n Oh, now those are some nice looking stickers, Blanca! %(_aquaticthemed[1]), Bill! And being %(_stickystickers[0]) brand, %(_stickystickers[1])!\n\n That sounds like a good deal to me, I'll have to get a few packs of my own while they're available!"
	"\1\b[22]Blanca, one of the questions we get asked frequently is how to choose colors when there are a lot available. Some of our items only have one or two colors, but others have a whole range! How do you approach this issue?\n\n Well, Bill, it really depends on what kind of look I'm building with my snail! I try not to think ""which of these %(RAND(9) + 1)0 colors am I going to pick"", and instead I think about what the main colors I want for this particular look are, and what I would find acceptable as an accent color. If an item is available in the colors I want, great! And if it's not, then I need to consider really carefully before I buy it.\n\n So what you're saying is that you avoid choice paralysis by knowing what colors you'll accept beforehand?\n\n Exactly right! For me, an item with a range of colors to choose from means that it's flexible for all kinds of looks. You just have to think about it the right way!\n\n That's interesting, I'll have to try that next time I'm outfitting a snail!"
	_boxfans1 = boxfans
	_boxfans2 = boxfans
	while _boxfans1 == _boxfans2
	{
		_boxfans2 = boxfans
	}
	"\1\b[22]And now we have a listener question about the %(_boxfans1) we were selling just last week!\n\n Oh? What did they have to say, Bill? %(ihopeenjoying)\n\n I'll read it out now, Blanca!\w8\w8\w8\n\n ""%(whysostinky)""\w8\w8\w8\w8\n\n ...\w8\w8\n\n ...\w8\w8\n\n %(snailpic) ...\w8\w8\w8\w8\n\n Well, that's a good question, Bill!\n\n It sure is, Blanca!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Wuh! Wahhh!\f[italic,default]\w8\w8\n\n We now move on to our next listener question! This one is about the upcoming sale we have on %(_boxfans2)..."
	"\1\b[22]Here we have a lovely moisturizing cream. If you've got a snail that's drying out, a moisturizing cream formulated for snails can be a great boon!\n\n It's true, Blanca! Using a mist bottle is all well and good, but if you can add some moisturizer into the mix it'll really help to keep your snail more comfortable over the long term."
	"\1\b[22]Next up, we've got this special bottle of ""Slime Away""! It's a patented formula guaranteed to get slime trails out of all sorts of materials, from cotton to leather!\n\n Ooh, you've got to be careful with this one, Bill! It can be wonderful for cleaning up trails in unwanted places, but you absolutely must make sure that no exploratory snails get into the area just after you've applied it. That would be a disaster!\n\n Indeed it would, Blanca. This is a wonder chemical, but you must be responsible with it. Nobody wants our little snail friends getting hurt!"
	
	_remotecontrol = remotecontrol
	"\1\b[22]The latest and greatest innovation from Tentacle Tech is here! They've just released a brand new snail-friendly %(_remotecontrol), which your snails will be able to use with ease!\n\n Ooh! That sounds wonderful, Bill. I can't tell you how many times I've looked at my %(_remotecontrol) and thought, ""I wish my snail could use this too"". This will be a serious improvement for my household!\n\n Mine as well, Blanca! New advancements from Tentacle Tech are always welcome, and I'm sure this new %(_remotecontrol) design will be a hit."
	"\1\b[22]Blanca, some of our listeners have expressed apprehension about spending so much lettuce on items to enhance their snail's performance. What's your take on the matter?\n\n Well, Bill, investing in your snail is really one of the best things you can do if you're serious about racing! Yes, it costs lettuce up front, but if you invest in the right items then you'll make all that lettuce back and then some. So I guess I would say not to be hesitant about it, just take a bit of time to plan before you start spending your hard earned greens!\n\n I have to say I agree whole-heartedly. And keep listening to our show, where we'll keep you updated on all the latest and greatest items that will be worth your while!"
	"\1\b[22]Blanca, we've been getting questions from our listeners about what forms of payment we can accept. In particular, it seems folks want to know about cabbage and spinach. What's our policy?\n\n Unfortunately, Bill, we can't accept cabbage or spinach, nor any other form of green besides lettuce! These alternative leaves must be converted to lettuce by exchanging them with an enthusiast, or some other means. What we \f[italic,1]do\f[italic,default] accept is direct lettuce payments, payments by lettuce card, or checks connected to a lettuce account!\n\n That makes sense to me! While other forms of payment are out there somewhere, they're not our business, so it's up to you to convert your greens before making a purchase."
	"\1\b[22]Blanca, our listeners want to know, do you have any tips on how to save lettuce and still get high-quality items?\n\n I sure do, Bill! It's all about coupons, coupons, coupons! Keep your radios tuned to our show, because we give out coupon codes throughout the day which can save you a lot on your purchases, big or small.\n\n It's true, we do! Besides that, I always keep a calculator on me so that I can figure out what items have the best lettuce-to-stats ratios. Sure it's a bit of extra work, but doing a few minutes of arithmetic is worth it to save some greens!\n\n I definitely agree with you there, Bill! Another thing to keep in mind is to know what colors you want before you shop, that way you don't end up buying multiples of the same item to achieve just the right look. It can really hurt your wallet if you have to buy the same item more than once.\n\n A very good point, and color coordination is so important if you're trying to have the most stylish snail!"
	"\1\b[22]Up next we have a collection of items to help enrich the lives of your snails during their downtime. We have an assortment of crossword puzzles, word searches, coloring books, and more!\n\n What I love most about these, Blanca, is that every part of them has been made with snails in mind. They're the right size for a snail to use, with those patented easy-turn pages, and best of all%(emdash)the pages are resistant to mucus stains!\n\n All very good features to have, Bill! I've let my snails help with my daily crossword in the paper sometimes, and mucus soaking through the pages has been a big issue. I think investing in these activity books will be just the thing to make everyone happy!"
	
	"\1\b[22]Bill, some of our listeners have been asking about whether it would be cost-effective to grow their own lettuce to spend. What advice would you have for them?\n\n Well, Blanca, it's difficult to give a single blanket statement! Whether it's cost-effective will depend on a lot of factors. Do you already have some of the needed supplies, or will you be starting from scratch? How much space have you got to work with? Do you have free time that you can fill with lettuce farming, or would you have to sacrifice time you would otherwise be spending preparing your snail for races?\n\n That's true, it'd do no good to neglect your snail's training since races also bring in lettuce! If you're already earning a fair amount from races, trying to farm lettuce might end up costing you more than it saves.\n\n Exactly right. It depends on your situation. For some folks, lettuce farming is a great supplemental income, and for others it's largely a waste of time. I'd encourage any of our listeners considering it to consult with a lettuce professional and see what's right for them!\n\n That being said, growing a few heads of lettuce for dietary purposes can be a great way to give your snails an extra fresh and flavorful treat. Don't confuse advice for monetary lettuce with advice for dietary lettuce!\n\n If you'd like to try growing your own dietary lettuce at home, we've got some great starter kits!" //I sort of wonder if this kind of thing belongs more in the variety show... idk it feels a bit wandery
	"\1\b[22]If you have a green thumb but all your house plants keep getting nibbled on, then these next items are for you! We've got all these lovely potted plants, except%(emdash)\w8oh my%(emdash)\w8these aren't real leaves!\n\n You're kidding! You really could have fooled me with these, I thought for sure they were real.\n\n When I first saw them, Bill, I thought the same! They're incredibly realistic and lifelike, but they're completely synthetic. Snails can crawl all over them if they like, but there's nothing worth eating here!\n\n Aw, I almost feel bad for the little guys. If you buy these, make sure you get your snails a little extra lettuce to stave off any disappointment!" //TODO i wonder if there's a better option for autopause and emdashes... i'm sure other dialogues could use the pauses as well
	"\1\b[22]Your snail deserves a special treat now and then, and boy have we got it for you!\n\n Oh? Do tell, Bill!\n\n Many snails have diets largely comprised of lettuce, dietary pellets, and the occasional store-bought vegetables or fruit. But what could be better than some home-grown foliage? Incomparable freshness, grown right in your own garden or windowsill!\n\n That does sound lovely! What's the best way to get started?\n\n Right here we've got some starter kits for all kinds of plants. From arugula and kale, to chives and basil, and much more besides! Mix and match, and try all the different types to find what your snail likes best. It's healthy, affordable, and it'll grow your bond like nothing else will!"
	"\1\b[22]Ooh, Bill, next up I want to have a look at these new poster designs we got in for %(TodaysChoice(FamousSnails))! Just look at how cool these are.\n\n Wow, that's a great design! That's a great angle to catch %(TodaysChoice(FamousSnails)) from. I almost feel like I'm there at the track watching it race!\n\n I know, it's wonderful, isn't it? You can really see how fast it's going, and that style it's got going on is impeccable. Someone put real thought and effort into every aspect of this!\n\n I'm blown away by the quality, Blanca. I know I'll be ordering some just as soon as I get home!"
	"\1\b[22]Bill, I've heard that %(TodaysChoice(FamousSnails)) will be releasing a new lineup of merchandise soon. Is it true?\n\n It \f[italic,1]is\f[italic,default] true, Blanca! I'm told that new designs are coming and will be available on t-shirts, mugs, socks, scarves, bags, pens, and so much more.\n\n Ooh, I can't wait to see it! If the new poster designs we've seen are a sign of what's to come, then this is going to be its best set of merchandise yet!"
	
	"\1\b[22]It's a common item, but it can't be overlooked! It's an everyday essential: a basket!\n\n These baskets just keep getting better and better, Blanca! This new design is the ultimate in snail comfort, with an adjustable strap made of soft pleather, and plenty of support for the basket so that it doesn't become unbalanced when it's filled.\n\n Every snail deserves a basket to carry around snacks or other items it wants to keep on hand! It's a great purchase, whether your snails are racers or not." //TODO i wonder if the baskets should have stats tho... hmm... i feel like a lettuce basket should make you go faster, anyway. i know i know, aesthetic choices, but..............
	"\1\b[22]Well folks, it's time for Blanca and I to take a little break!\n\n But don't go away, we'll be back soon with more deals just for you!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Bye bye! Be back!\f[italic,default]\e:chain=chain.blanca_bill_break"
	"\1\b[22]Here's something special I really like, Blanca. It's a premium photo album, which you can fill with pictures of your snail!\n\n Ooh, that looks lovely! I would love to fill this up with pictures of my darling %(_snailname).\n\n I personally like to buy an album for each snail. It serves as a collection of memories of our time spent together, and it can also be a great way to show progress and improvement over time!\n\n That's a great idea! I'll have to get some right away."
	"\1\b[22]Blanca, I've been hearing rumors are going around that if you offer %(carrots) as part of your payment at checkout, you can get a discount. Is that true?\n\n No Bill, it isn't! We don't accept any vegetables except lettuce as payment, although we do accept multiple forms of lettuce such as direct lettuce payments, lettuce cards, and checks from lettuce bank accounts. Other fruits and vegetables sure are delicious, but not valid currency, I'm afraid!\n\n I had thought as much. If you have other plants that you need to convert to lettuce, you'd better find an enthusiast who will buy them off of you!" //TODO i've used "direct lettuce payments" here and in another one above in reference to "cash"... "lettuce in hand"...?
	"\1\b[22]Up next are these special gel pens we have!\n\n Oh, now what's special about these, Bill?\n\n Quite simple, Blanca! Unlike most gel pens, these ones are super resistant to mucus! You can once more jot down notes on paper, without having to worry about an errant snail smudging up your message and rendering it unreadable.\n\n That's a good idea! Do they also have mucus-resistant paper?\n\n They certainly do! A worthwhile investment if you ask me, the extra cost really helps to protect whatever it is you want to write down."
	
	"\1\b[22]Sponsors who get cuddly with their snails will love this next one! We've got the new formula of DentaStix%(emdash)\w8the all natural sticks that will clean your snail's radula as it rasps away at them! Snails love the taste, and you'll love your snail's minty fresh breath.\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Wuh? Waaaah!\f[italic,default]\n\n Ooh, Bill that sounds great! A tasty treat \f[italic,1]and\f[italic,default] fresh breath after? I almost wish I could clean \f[italic,1]my\f[italic,default] teeth that way!\n\n Tell me about it! Come on, DentaStix, invent a human formula so we can match with our snails! Hahaha."
	"\1\b[22]Here's one that I'm sure a lot of snails and sponsors alike will really appreciate%(emdash)\w8a snail playground! Got an energetic snail that keeps exploring in places you wish it wouldn't, or worse, getting outside and wandering off? It might need more enrichment in its day! Get it one of these handy playsets, and it can get that energy out in a safe and constructive manner.\n\n This is a great item Blanca. Just look at all those tunnels, slides, climbing walls... I wish I had a playset like this in my size, I'd never leave it!\n\n Hahaha, I know the feeling! But sadly, they only make them for snails, as far as I know. And I'm sure they're going to make some snails very, very happy, so call in now and get your order placed before these things fly off the shelves and out of stock!"
	"\1\b[22]%(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Hubop! Hah!\f[italic,default]\n\n Haha, Bill, I think %(_snailname) is excited for the %(boxfans) we have over there!\n\n I think you're right, Blanca. It's certainly got an eye for a good deal, since those have just gone on sale for %(ANY(10,15,20,25,30,35,40))% off!\n\n Ooh, that would make any snail happy, wouldn't it? Thanks for the help, %(_snailname)!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Woohoo!\f[italic,default]"
	"\1\b[22]As a reminder for folks, we've always got Super Snail's Snail Tracks ice cream available in pints and quarts! 100% of all proceeds go to the various charities and programs that Super Snail supports!\n\n Which one is it currently, Blanca?\n\n Let's see... Looks like it's %(TodaysChoice(safesnailsociety)) this week, Bill!\n\n Oh, now that's a great cause if I've ever heard of one. I think it's time I stock up my freezer with some more Snail Tracks!\n\n Hahaha, you said it!"
	"\1\b[22]Bill, do you hand wash your snails?\n\n Of course I do, Blanca! It's the best way to care for their shells, and to make sure their equipment doesn't get damaged. Why do you ask?\n\n Well, I thought you might be interested in this new set of %(starshaped) sponges we just got in! They come in an assortment of colors, and they're made with all the latest sponge technology for a gentle, but thorough, clean.\n\n Oho! Yes, that I am definitely interested in. Sponges wear out after a while, you know. It's important to keep your sponges in top condition for the best clean!"
	
	_pelletsdemonstration = SPLIT(TodaysChoice(pelletsdemonstration),"|")
	"\1\b[22]%(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Wah! Wahh!\f[italic,default]\n\n Oh? %(_snailname), we've already talked about those %(boxfans) on today's show!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Gubuh! Gimme!\f[italic,default]\n\n ... Blanca, I think %(_snailname) might be hungry!\n\n Ooh, you know, I think you're right Bill! In that case, how about a practical demonstration of our next product? %(_pelletsdemonstration[0]) make a quick and easy snack for your snail, and are packed full of nutrition!\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Crunch crunch.\f[italic,default]\n\n See, look at how happy it is. %(_pelletsdemonstration[1])\n\n Very true, Bill! When it comes to supplementing my snail's diet with pellets, %(_pelletsdemonstration[0]) are always my #1 pick. %(_pelletsdemonstration[2])\n\n It's an important consideration! Food choices really have to be examined from a number of angles, %(_pelletsdemonstration[3])\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Chomp chew.\f[italic,default]\n\n That's the sound of a satisfied snail enjoying %(_pelletsdemonstration[0]), folks. Buy some today!"
	"\1\b[22]Bill, have you got a well-thought-out housing solution for all your snails?\n\n You know what Blanca, I've never really thought about it! What have you got for us?\n\n It's the latest and greatest snail habitat innovation: SnailPartments! This prefabricated lattice of squares can be placed along any wall in your home to instantly transform it into a luxury snail habitat!\n\n Oh wow, now that is convenient. My snails usually stay in one tank all together, but now they'll each get their own cozy room. It's brilliant!\n\n Exactly! And if you order the special premium model, you can hook it up to your water supply, and each snail can use the mister built into the top of its room to mist itself whenever desired.\n\n That sounds like the peak of snail comfort. Why doesn't my room have a built in mister?\n\n Ooh I know, it sounds lovely. I'm certain this is going to be a hot item, so be sure to order yours quick, everyone, before they're gone!"
	"\1\b[22]Blanca, have a look at this!\n\n Ooh, what is it, Bill?\n\n It's my favorite new item for snail enrichment in the home. The FastTrack! It's a quick and easy practice race track that you can deploy in any room, any time!\n\n Oh, interesting! How does it work?\n\n Simply unfold the smooth plastic track and let it click into place, set it down in your desired location, attach optional accessories like these little flags and a checkered banner at the finish line, and set your snail inside! It can go around and around as much as it likes, and you can cheer it on from the side.\n\n Wow, it seems like a simple way to keep your snails entertained, and even get in a little more practice for races!\n\n It sure is! I've been using it with my snails, and it's been a huge hit. Why, I've had to buy a dozen of them just to keep up with the demand!\n\n Amazing! I'll have to get a few of them to try for myself." //Snails need enrichment beyond just racing............
	"\1\b[22]If your everyday essentials need a little more pizzazz, we've got you covered. Check out these all-new misting bottles in a variety of colors and patterns from MultiMist!\n\n Dozens of colors to choose from, and you can pick options such as two-tone, plaid, racing stripes, and glitter. Each one has a great ergonomic handle to keep you comfortable while you comfort your snail friend!\n\n That's right, Bill! These spray bottles really are top-notch, premium products. Buy some for your snails today! Brighten up each snail's day with a bottle in it's favorite color.\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Wahoo! Water!\f[italic,default]\n\n Aw, now that's real love, folks!"
	"\1\b[22]Now Bill, you were saying you wanted to promote some %(boxfans) today?\n\n Yes Blanca, we've got a really great deal going on where%(emdash)\n\n %(snailpic) \f[italic,1]Wah! Wubah!? \f[color,disable]Crash.\f[color,default]\f[italic,default]\n\n Oh no! %(_snailname), are you alright? \f[color,disable]What were you doing over here? You poor dear...\f[color,default]\n\n ... Well, looks like that deal is going, going, gone! That's a reminder for all of us that a good deal never lasts long, so if you hear us talk about something you just can't live without, get your orders in quickly before it's too late. You never know \f[italic,1]what\f[italic,default] could happen, hahaha!"
}

