	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Duh nuh duh nuh duh nuh DUH, duh duh duh do, dah dah dah, dah DAH!%(note2)" //Sninematic
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Do do, do be do be, do do do bah bah~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Do do, be be do do, bah bah bum bum bah~%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Wah wah wah, wah wah wah wah!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Wah wah, wah wah, wah wah wahhhhh!%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Do de do, do de do~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Do de do de do, dah dah~%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Wop wop bah do bah dah do, wop wop de be de!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)De wop do do de de bah, bup dop do be do!%(note2)" //Snrap
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Wup wup do do be be do, de wop wup do bah de!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Wup wup do be do do dah, de wup wup bah de dah!%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Wop wop! Do be dah be dah, wup!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Wop wop! Do dah be de dah!%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Do be de do be de do be de DO, DAH DAH, DO BE DO DAH!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Dah dah dah dah, dah dah dah dah.%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Do be do be do, do do do do, do be do...%(note2)" //Snlassical
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Do do dop do, do do dop do~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Do be do dop do, do be do do~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Do be do be? Do do~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Do dop be dop do be do~%(note2)" //Spop
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Do do, do do, do, do do DO!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Do be do be do be do be do be do do, do do do be do dodo do do, do be do dodo do dodo do, do do be do be do be do be do~%(note2)" //Snmerry-go-round which is really just more snlassical, don't @ me i like RCT2, god do you think they have snail themed amusement parks... or like... amusement parks that are snail sized and made for snails
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Do dop, dah be dah do dop, do be dah dah do dop, dah be do, bop bop do~%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Do do do be, do do do be do be do be, do be do be do do do do be do be do~%(note2)" //god help you if you try to interpret what this actually is. feel free to send me a guess and you'll win me sending you a cookie emoji if you're right. man will i even remember myself after a month?
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Do do be do be do do do do be, do be do do be do do be~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Do do do be do be do do do do be, do do do do be do do be~%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Wah wah, wah wah wah wah!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Wah wah wah wah, wah wah wah wahhh!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Wahhhh wah wah wah! Wah wah wah!%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Do do bop, do wop de do bop, dop de do~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Dop dop do bop, do do do be do be wop de do~%(note2)"
	
	"\1\b[20]Now back to our foot tapping, shell cracking, Boogie Down Music Hour!\n\n %(note1)Do wop~ Do be do be da do~%(note2)"
	
	//Actual lyrics
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Ooooo be my racing baby~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Ooooo be my winning bet~%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Watch them zip across the track~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Oh, these snails are such a thrill~%(note2)" //resisting the urge to put "also a delicious snack"...
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Ohh look on down the line~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Here comes that shiny shell, claiming the fastest time~%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Go snail racers, go!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Go snail racers, go!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Give it everything you've got,%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Go snail racers, go!%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Oh, don't let a little loss hold you back~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Oh, you'll have another chance on the track~%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Snails, snails, buy em by the dozen~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)You'll find that perfect racer, the one that'll have 'em buzzin'~%(note2)" //\n\n %(note1)They train up quick, so there's no sense in rushin'!%(note2)\n\n %(note1)And if it don't work out, you can put em in the oven~%(note2) Is............. is it too much :rofl: I could snip the second half... i feel like it might be tooooo dark but it does make me laugh
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Grow that lettuce nice and tall~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Plentiful gardens help us all~%(note2)" //does lettuce grow tall...
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Ooh, look at that spiral go round and round~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)There's no better snail to be found~%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Don't let your snails scatter around~%(note2)\n\n %(note1)Keep them in, all safe and sound~%(note2)"
	"\1\b[20]%(note1)Let those lil guys take the lead, cuz these snails got a need for speed!%(note2)"
	//"\1\b[20]"
	
	//DJ
	_somesnail = SnailNameGenerator(,"not alliteration")
	//TODO this dialogue needs an embed tag or something so that repeating it doesn't draw a new lyric... maybe I could just grab a random index I guess, since it doesn't need to rotate like the traffic stuff. NOTE: this ALSO has to apply to the variety show when we get there!
	"\1\b[22]And now for something special, folks! A little snail called %(_somesnail) is here in the studio with us today, and it's going to perform a song that it wrote itself. Take it away, %(_somesnail)!\n\n %(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)\n\n \f[italic,1]\![embed,OnSnailSong]\f[italic,default]\n\n %(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)%(note1)\_w[2000]\n\n Aw, that was lovely. Thank you for that wonderful performance, %(_somesnail), and we hope you'll come back to the studio again someday to sing another song!"
	"\1\b[22]It's that time of the day again, folks,%(br)it's time to put in your music requests! Starting next hour, I play nothing but what you send me; you control the show!\n\n Get out those phones, send me a message on the snailernet, use our app; whatever way you wanna get it to me, get it to me and I'll play out the snail tunes you've been itching for."
	"\1\b[22]How's everyone feeling out there? These tunes are hot today, yowza!\n\n We'll get right back to it in a moment, but I want to take this time to remind everyone about the %(TodaysChoices(charityevent1))"
	"\1\b[22]Woo! How's everyone doing, feeling awake? What a way to start the day off with some classic tunes that really get your blood pumping! I don't know about you, but all these greatest snail hits make my feet feel like they gotta MOVE!\n\n Stay tuned, it's time to pause and thank our sponsors, but we'll be back in a minute with all your favorites and more on 103.7, \f[italic,1]Mollusk Music\f[italic,default]!" //TODO i wonder if "start the day off" ought to be replaced based on the runtime... "start the day off", "get us through the afternoon", "keep us awake through the evening"...
	"\1\b[22]Alright alright alright, how was that for a great song? It's a shame you all can't see what it's like here in the studio,%(br)'cuz every time we play that one I end up rocking out no matter what else is going on.\n\n That being said, it's that part of the hour where I remind you guys about the %(TodaysChoices(charityevent2))"
	"\1\b[22]Woohoo! Doesn't that one just make you wanna dance no matter where you are? Just last week I was %(inmycar). It was really something else.\n\n More great tunes like that are coming up soon, so don't touch that dial!%(br)We'll be back in a minute after a word from our generous sponsors."
	"\1\b[22]Hey hey hey, check it out guys, we've still got that %(TodaysChoices(charityevent3))"
	"\1\b[22]Who's ready for some more rockin' snail songs? We've got a great lineup this next hour, so crank up the volume and share these beats with all your neighbors!"
	"\1\b[22]Yahoo, today's tracks have been absolutely scorching hot! We hope all you snails and snail fans out there are having a great time, and we'll be back with more after a quick word from our sponsors that help us keep the show on the air!"
	"\1\b[22]Ahh, that's a good song, isn't it? One of the all-time greats, it really is. You can feel the energy zipping around the room whenever we play it out.\n\n We've got more great tunes in store for you this hour, so stay with us! And if you'd like to hear your favorites starting next hour, make sure to send in your requests now! Give us a call, send it to me on the snailernet, send a request in on our app; however you can get it to me, get it to me and I'll make it happen!"
	"\1\b[22]How's everyone doing out there, has that last song got you movin' and groovin'? It's sure made its way to my feet, let me tell you. I feel like I could %(danceallnight)!\n\n Let's keep that energy going with this next tune on 103.7, \f[italic,1]Mollusk Music\f[italic,default]. Take it away!"
	"\1\b[22]Well, that really was a blast from the past, wasn't it? We've pulled out some old songs from our archives to play for you today. They might be a bit older than our standard fare, but as they say, absence makes the heart grow fonder!\n\n Look forward to some more deep cuts throughout the show today! And if you can correctly guess what artists we have in our lineup, you'll be entered to win a prize, so give us a call and get your guesses in!"
	"\1\b[22]How's that for a nostalgic tune, huh? We're dusting off the old archives today, so get ready for some vintage memories this show! And don't forget that next hour will be songs picked by you, our listeners. If there's a deep cut you'd like to hear in particular, send us a request and if we've got it%(br)I'll make sure we play it just for you!"
	"\1\b[22]Woo! How about that weather, huh? We've got some great tunes for a day like today, so stick with us while we hear a word from our sponsors, and we'll be back with some weather-appropriate songs to jam out to!"
	"\1\b[22]What a powerful song, am I right? The kind you can't help but sing along to, whether you know the words or not, hahaha!\n\n More like that coming up right now on 103.7, \f[italic,1]Mollusk Music\f[italic,default]. And after this next song I'll tell you more about that %(TodaysChoices(charityevent4))!"
	"\1\b[22]How about that. Talk about a timeless song, I can't imagine a day will come when we don't play that track every show. Ah, it just hits you real good when that last chorus comes in, incredible.\n\n We're going to get right back into some sweet tunes, but stick around, we've got that %(TodaysChoices(charityevent5)), and we'll have more details for you after this next song!"
	"\1\b[22]Woo, bust out those dance moves, these greatest hits just keep coming!\n\n And we're right back into it, so don't touch that dial. You're listening to%(br)103.7, \f[italic,1]Mollusk Music\f[italic,default]."
	"\1\b[22]Man, I can feel everyone's excitement from here! Who's ready for this next tune?\n\n We'll get into it in just a moment, but as a quick reminder, next hour we'll be playing out your requests, so make sure you get 'em in! Call in, message me on the snailernet, talk to us through our app. However you can get your request in, do it and it just might get played out next hour!"
	"\1\b[22]What a legendary song. Truly genre-defying, I remember when it first came out and everyone went wild over those thrilling harmonies.\n\n I want to hear from you guys, what songs from your childhood stick most firmly in your memory? Send 'em in to us, and we might just play them out if it's been a while!"
	"\1\b[22]Ah, I never get tired of these snail songs. There's nothing quite like hearing a thousand snails raise up their voice in one glorious chorus, or hearing a well-tuned group of snails singing in perfect harmony.\n\n What's your favorite kind of snail song? Send in your votes today via our app, or on the snailernet, and let us know!"
}

//The Cheetah
//Snail Talk
RadioStation.Variety_Show : nonoverlap_pool
{
	//"\1\b[20]wow these poems sure are hot!"
	_humancaller = HumanName
	"\1\b[22]Looks like we've got a caller on the line... This one's from %(_humancaller) of %(snailcity). %(_humancaller), what's the word?\n\n Yeah, hi, uh. I was wondering if you were aware that \f[italic,1]Snack Shack\f[italic,default] is having a deal where if you buy one snail sized shake you get a human sized shake free—\n\n Aaand that's enough of that. Sorry about the interruption, listeners! The Cheetah is here to keep unvetted advertisements out of your ears!"
	"\1\b[22]Let's take another caller... %(_humancaller) of %(snailcity), you're on the air!\n\n Hello, The Cheetah, I'm excited to be here!\n\n It's always great to hear from our listeners. What's going on with you and your snails today, %(_humancaller)?\n\n Oh! Right! Yeah, I could use some advice.\n\n Mhm, mhm, let's get the storytime. \n\n So, for a while now, one of my snails has been sneaking into the garage outside of maintenance time. Which wasn't too much of a problem at first, but lately it's been hiding in the toolboxes! I've tried everything I can think of to get it to stop. I'm worried it'll get hurt...\n\n This sounds like a tricky one. Tell us, what's your snail doing when you find it in the toolbox?\n\n It crawls all over the wrenches. They end up practically dripping with mucus!\n\n And its enclosure, it's got plenty of things to climb on in there, right?\n\n Of course! Only the best snail safe sticks. It doesn't use them much, though...\n\n Try this: take out some of those sticks, and get yourself a nice thick chain to hang in there. Your snail might be looking for a particular texture against its foot. Better for you to provide it than leave your snail to find it on its own. Give us another call and let us know how it goes.\n\n Okay! Will do!"
}

//Tim Gulls / Sy Lance
//Calming Crackles
RadioStation.ASMR : nonoverlap_pool
{
	//Pick a random jockey of the day, for a bit more variety on this station. Note to self - if we add more this has to be manually added to the aigraph also - INCLUDING the "current dialogues" counter
	_candidates = IARRAY
	_jockeys = ("Tim Gulls","Sy Lance")
	_today = TodaysChoice(_jockeys)
	if _today == "Sy Lance"
	{
		_candidates = ASMR.dialogues.sylance
	}
	else //Tim Gulls - the OG
	{
		_candidates = ASMR.dialogues.timgulls
	}
	
	//This setup is so that we can avoid writing all those tags for each ASMR dialogue, but also so that it doesn't break chains...
	for _i = 0; _i < ARRAYSIZE(_candidates); _i++
	{
		_candidates[_i] = "\1\b[20]\f[italic,1]\f[color,disable]" + _candidates[_i]
		if "\e" _in_ _candidates[_i]; _candidates[_i] = REPLACE(_candidates[_i],"\e","\f[color,default]\f[italic,default]\e")
		else; _candidates[_i] += "\f[color,default]\f[italic,default]"
	}
	
	parallel _candidates
}

